  "id": "Compound::DB00274 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Cefmetazole is likely to interact with Slc15a1 through a shared functional pathway involving Slc15a2. The evidence suggests that Cefmetazole binds to Slc15a2, which participates in multiple transport activities, including proton-dependent peptide transport and oligopeptide transport. These activities are all part of a broader mechanism involving Slc15a1, indicating that Cefmetazole may influence the function of Slc15a1 through its interaction with Slc15a2. The high scores in the paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of how Cefmetazole affects Slc15a1 remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Slc15a2 as a potential mediator in the interaction between Cefmetazole and Slc15a1.",
